    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n106139" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑάλη</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκώληξ</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, who also cites <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑάλεται:</span></b> 
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκωληκιᾷ</span>: these are prob. dial.
			forms of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐλή, εὐλάζει</span> (which he
			also explains by <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκωληκιᾷ</span>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
